    'body'        => <<<'HTML'
<p>In most Texas property claims, you can bring in a public adjuster at any point before the claim is finally resolved: before filing, after the inspection, after a low offer, and often even after you have been paid. It is usually too late once you have signed a full release, once a deadline in your policy or in Texas law has passed, or once a lawsuit is underway and an attorney is running the case.</p>
<p>Earlier is easier. A public adjuster who sees the damage before repairs and before the first inspection has more to work with than one who arrives after the roof has been replaced. But "later" is not the same as "too late."</p>

<div class="keyfacts">
